Article 4 (Duties)
(1) Technical examiners shall perform any of the following duties:
1. Giving advice to the court whenever requested by the presiding judge on technical or specialized issues in a case;
2. Reviewing litigation records under orders from the presiding judge and submitting to the court opinions concerning the evaluation of technical evidence, examination and review of factual issues, and related specialist knowledge, or orally reporting the results of research or opinions;
3. With permission from the presiding judge or a commissioned judge, questioning persons involved in the proceedings about technical matters during oral arguments or preparatory proceedings (excluding cases concerning trademarks);
4. With permission from the presiding judge, stating opinions on technical matters in the course of deliberations (excluding cases concerning trademarks).
(2) In the case of paragraph (1) 4, the presiding judge may require a technical examiner to submit in advance in writing the opinions to be stated during deliberations.
(3) Written opinions submitted and statements made by technical examiners under paragraph (1) 2 and 4 shall not be made public.
